<title>LEBANON: Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 568.4 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Beirut weekly T-bill issue raises 568.4 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's weekly treasury bill issue of November 28 raised 568.4 billion Lebanese pounds, the finance ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The previous issue raised 477.9 billion pounds.</p>
<p>The new issue posted a nominal surplus of subscription against maturity of 374 billion pounds. It raised the following amounts (in billions of pounds, previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term			  Yield		    Amount</p>
<p>    Three months	    14.39 (14.43)	   48.7  (71.4)</p>
<p>    Six months		16.55 (16.67)	   94.6  (52.1)</p>
<p>    12 months		 17.57 (17.57)	   91.9  (84.2)</p>
<p>    24 months		 21.00 (21.26)	  333.2 (270.2)</p>
<p>The Lebanese pound closed at 1,554 to the U.S. dollar on Monday from 1,554.25 a week earlier and 1,599.5 a year ago.</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 645456</p>
